# Ratatoille's camp talks (story/camp_talk.gd): offered after a Long Rest once the opening `if` holds; each plays
# once. Quest: A Seat at the Table (narrative/companions/table.dialogue). The table talk is the quest's ending. The
# file offers its first talk that holds: when he's Strained or Doubtful (story/approval.gd), those first; then the
# quest's; then Warm, Close and Devoted.

# --- After Strahd called Ratatoille to kneel at the night visit (strahd/visits:night_kneel) ---------------------------

~ talk_knelt
if name:ratatoille and flag.strahd_knelt == "ratatoille"
-> knelt
endif
-> END

~ knelt
Narrator: Ratatoille is cooking breakfast with tremendous concentration, though there's very little to cook and nobody is hungry.
interject name:ratatoille: He said I wished to be taken seriously. Then he had me fold my blanket and walk to him like a waiter with an empty plate.
interject name:ratatoille: I am a diviner. I saw nothing coming. Nothing.
* Nobody could have foreseen that. -> knelt_foresee
* Next time we'll be ready for him. -> knelt_ready

~ knelt_foresee
interject name:ratatoille: I can foresee breakfast. Breakfast I will foresee, and it will be excellent, and you will all eat it. Sit.
approve ratatoille +3: You told me nobody could have foreseen Strahd's visit
-> END

~ knelt_ready
interject name:ratatoille: Next time I sleep with the skillet. I want to see his face when I take him seriously.
approve ratatoille +2: You said we'd be ready for Strahd next time
-> END

# --- When he's lost faith in the party (approval) ----------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_strained
if name:ratatoille and approval.ratatoille <= strained
-> strained
endif
-> END

~ strained
Narrator: There's no supper tonight. Ratatoille hands round the rations cold, still in their paper, and sits apart with his spellbook shut on his knees.
interject name:ratatoille: I'm not cooking. Don't ask me to. I can't cook for people when it doesn't taste right in my mouth to do it.
interject name:ratatoille: I learned magic so people would sit with me. Then I found people who would. And now I look at the table and I don't know whether I want to sit at it.
* Then help us set it right. -> strained_right
* We're sorry, Ratatoille. -> strained_sorry
* Suit yourself. -> strained_cold

~ strained_right
interject name:ratatoille: Kindness first. Then cleverness. Then fire. That's the correct order of operations. You've been doing it backwards.
interject name:ratatoille: Tomorrow I'll cook. Something simple. Bread. You can't lie with bread.
approve ratatoille +10: You asked me to help set it right
-> END

~ strained_sorry
interject name:ratatoille: Thank you. I accept. Provisionally. Like a soufflé: we'll see if it rises.
approve ratatoille +5: You told me you were sorry
-> END

~ strained_cold
Narrator: He nods without looking up and opens his spellbook to a page he obviously isn't reading.
approve ratatoille -6: You told me to suit myself
-> END

~ talk_doubt
if name:ratatoille and approval.ratatoille == doubtful
-> doubt
endif
-> END

~ doubt
Narrator: Ratatoille is cooking tonight, which is normal. He's cooking badly, which isn't. The stew has caught on the bottom and he hasn't noticed.
interject name:ratatoille: Non, it's fine. I'm distracted. A chef is permitted to be distracted once a century.
interject name:ratatoille: May I say something without anyone putting a frog in my soup? Lately I don't like who we're being. It's like a sauce that's split. You keep stirring, and you can't tell when it went wrong, and then it's just wrong.
interject name:ratatoille: At the academy I kept my head down and agreed with whoever was loudest. I came here to stop doing that. So. I'm not agreeing.
* Good. Tell us when we're wrong. -> doubt_good
* What would you do differently? -> doubt_what
* Keep stirring, Rat. -> doubt_stir

~ doubt_good
interject name:ratatoille: Oh. I... yes. I will. I'll be insufferable. I'll be extremely insufferable. Thank you.
approve ratatoille +6: You asked me to tell you when we're wrong
-> END

~ doubt_what
interject name:ratatoille: Think first. Be kind second. Fireball third. In that order, always. Nobody listens to the order.
approve ratatoille +3: You asked me what I'd do differently
-> END

~ doubt_stir
interject name:ratatoille: Of course. Stirring. I'm very good at stirring and keeping quiet. I'd hoped to stop.
approve ratatoille -4: You told me to keep stirring and keep quiet
-> END

# --- His quest ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_refectory
if name:ratatoille and quest.a_seat_at_the_table
-> refectory
endif
-> END

~ refectory
Narrator: Ratatoille is doing something complicated to tonight's rations with a pinch of salt, a pinch of something from a twist of paper, and a great deal of concentration. It smells unreasonably good.
interject name:ratatoille: Don't watch. I can't work when people watch. Watch a little.
* Where did you learn to cook like that? -> refectory_where
* Why magic, then, and not cooking? -> refectory_why

~ refectory_where
interject name:ratatoille: Under a pastry table. My family keeps a kitchen in a river town. Eleven of us, one kitchen. I was the one nobody noticed, so I was the one who saw how everything was done.
-> refectory_why

~ refectory_why
interject name:ratatoille: At the academy I sat alone at meals for nine years. Nine. Do you know how long that is for an elf? It isn't long. It felt long.
interject name:ratatoille: Then one day a boy called Aubert put a frog in my soup, and I lost my temper, and I threw fire across the refectory. Not at him. Mostly not at him. The curtains were never the same.
interject name:ratatoille: The next day, people sat with me. A whole table of them. Asking about fire.
interject name:ratatoille: So I learned more fire. And then other things. Divination, which is very prestigious, you know, it's the senior school. Titles. Circles. Nobody sits alone at the senior school.
interject name:ratatoille: And then I heard about the Wizard of Wines, and I thought: there's a man who's done both. Magic and the table. And nobody would dare laugh at him. I'm going to learn from him, and then nobody will ever laugh at me again.
* People are sitting with you now. -> refectory_now
* Nobody here is laughing. -> refectory_now

~ refectory_now
interject name:ratatoille: That's because they haven't tasted it yet. Here. Taste this. No, wait. Now. Now taste it.
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: BARK AND BONES. Rat. RAT.
interject name:ratatoille: That's good? That's a good noise?
elif name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Oh. Oh, that's lovely. That's the best thing I've had since the mutton soup at the Wheatsheaf, and I cried at the Wheatsheaf.
endif
interject name:ratatoille: It's nothing. It's rations. Anybody could do it. Nobody's going to do it, but anybody could.
approve ratatoille +2: You sat with me while I cooked
-> END

~ talk_recipes
if name:ratatoille and quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= a_winery and flag.eva_truth_teller != "ratatoille"
-> recipes
endif
-> END

~ recipes
Narrator: Ratatoille has his spellbook open on his knees and is reading it the way some people read letters from home.
interject name:ratatoille: You can look. It's all right. Everyone's going to find out eventually.
Narrator: The spellbook is laid out like a cookery book. Every spell has its ingredients listed down the margin, its method numbered, and a note at the bottom headed "Serving suggestion". Fireball's says: "Do not serve indoors."
interject name:ratatoille: I'd rather cook than cast. I always would. I'm good at magic, I'm very good, I'm going to be extremely good. But I'd rather cook. When I cook, I'm not trying to be anything.
interject name:ratatoille: That's a terrible thing for a wizard to say. Don't tell the Wizard of Wines. Wherever he is. If he exists. Whoever he was.
* Maybe you can be both. -> recipes_both
* Your secret's safe. -> recipes_safe

~ recipes_both
interject name:ratatoille: That's what I wanted. That's the whole reason I came. And it turned out to be a farm. A very good farm. I'm not bitter. I'm a little bitter. It's good wine.
approve ratatoille +2: You told me I could be a wizard and a cook both
-> END

~ recipes_safe
interject name:ratatoille: Thank you. Not that it's a secret. It's just private. There's a difference. One's for hiding, and one's for keeping.
approve ratatoille +2: You kept my spellbook's secret
-> END

~ talk_table
# Approval (story/approval.gd): Strained or worse, and he doesn't lay the cloth until it's mended; Close or better, and
# the supper is a feast that stays with everyone.
if name:ratatoille and quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= the_wizard_found and not (quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= his_own_table) and not (approval.ratatoille <= strained)
-> table
endif
-> END

~ table
Narrator: Ratatoille sends everyone away from the fire for an hour and won't say why. When you're let back, there's a cloth laid on the ground, and a supper on it that has no business existing in this valley: something roasted, something in a sauce, bread that's still warm, and a little pastry at each place with an apricot in it.
if name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Those are my apricots. You got them out of my cart. ...They're beautiful. Keep going.
endif
interject name:ratatoille: Sit. Everybody sit. Sit with me. That's an order. I'm a diviner of the... I'm a cook. Sit.
if quest.a_seat_at_the_table >= the_masters_word
interject name:ratatoille: Mordenkainen told me status is a coat. Anyone can wear it, and it keeps nobody warm. I've been thinking about that. He's right. He's a horrible old man and he's right.
else
interject name:ratatoille: The wizard on the mountain played dragonchess against nobody for a year. The greatest wizard of the age, maybe, and nobody sat with him either. I've been thinking about that.
endif
if flag.ratatoille_zantras_refused
interject name:ratatoille: And a thing in amber offered me the whole world looking at me, forever, and I very nearly said yes, and the only reason I didn't was that I already had this. Which I hadn't noticed. Until right then.
endif
if flag.ratatoille_refused_strahd
interject name:ratatoille: And the devil himself offered me a tower, and I told him I already had a table. I meant this one. I meant you.
endif
Narrator: He stands up. He looks round at all of you, and visibly loses his nerve, and visibly gets it back.
interject name:ratatoille: Ratatoille. Cook. And wizard. In that order.
Narrator: He sits down again, very fast, and goes very pink, and starts serving before anyone can say anything.
if approval.ratatoille >= close
Narrator: There's a name piped on each pastry in burnt sugar, one per person, spelled wrong only once. Nobody mentions which. The supper sits warm in all of you right through the next day, like a hand on the back.
interject name:ratatoille: I cooked for the Martikovs because they let me. I used to cook so that people would sit with me. This one I cooked because you're mine. That's different. I didn't know it was different.
inspire party: ate Ratatoille's supper at his own table
endif
quest a_seat_at_the_table his_own_table
approve ratatoille +8: You sat at my table
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Hear, hear!
interject name:thistle: COOK!
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: Bless this table, and the one who made it.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: In that order. I'll allow it.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Can I sell these? I'm not going to. I just want to know if I can.
-> END

# --- As he comes to trust the party (approval) --------------------------------------------------------------------

~ talk_warm
if name:ratatoille and approval.ratatoille >= warm and level >= 3
-> warm
endif
-> END

~ warm
Narrator: Ratatoille has drawn three circles in the dirt with a stick and is standing in the middle one, looking very pleased with himself.
interject name:ratatoille: The Circles. First Circle: cantrips. Second Circle: anything that explodes. Third Circle: me. I'm establishing them. Somebody has to.
interject name:ratatoille: You may join, if you like. The entrance requirement is that you eat whatever I cook without asking what's in it.
* What's in it? -> warm_what
* (Step into the circle.) -> warm_join
* Can I be in a Fourth Circle? -> warm_fourth

~ warm_what
interject name:ratatoille: You've failed the entrance examination. Wonderful. Nobody's ever failed before. It's very prestigious.
approve ratatoille +1: You asked what's in it, which nobody ever does
-> END

~ warm_join
interject name:ratatoille: Welcome to the Third Circle. You're the first member who isn't me. ...It's mushrooms. It's always mushrooms. Don't tell anyone.
approve ratatoille +3: You joined the Third Circle
-> END

~ warm_fourth
interject name:ratatoille: There is no Fourth Circle. ...There is now. You're it. It's above mine. Don't let it go to your head.
approve ratatoille +2: You asked to join a circle above mine
-> END

~ talk_close
if name:ratatoille and approval.ratatoille >= close and level >= 5
-> close
endif
-> END

~ close
Narrator: Ratatoille is making a tart tonight, and making it badly: doing a step wrong, stopping, doing it right, as if he were arguing with somebody who isn't there.
interject name:ratatoille: It's my grandmother's. She makes it every feast day, and every feast day she tells me I'm doing the crust wrong. I'm doing it her way tonight. I wanted to see if I could stand it.
interject name:ratatoille: Before I left, I told my whole family I was going to be apprenticed to the greatest wizard of the age. My brothers laughed. My grandmother said, "He'll be back in the kitchen by spring," and they all laughed harder.
interject name:ratatoille: And the thing is, I want to go back to the kitchen. I want to go home and cook. And I'm terrified that means she was right, and I'll only ever be the boy under the pastry table.
* The kitchen's where you're best. That isn't small. -> close_best
* You can go home a wizard and a cook. -> close_both
* Your grandmother doesn't get to decide that. -> close_decide

~ close_best
interject name:ratatoille: Isn't it? No. No, it isn't. Nobody ever says that. Everybody says "only" a cook.
approve ratatoille +3: You told me the kitchen isn't small
-> close_end

~ close_both
interject name:ratatoille: Both. Yes. Ratatoille, Diviner of the... no. Just both. Both is enough. Both is a lot, actually.
approve ratatoille +3: You told me I can go home a wizard and a cook
-> close_end

~ close_decide
interject name:ratatoille: She does, though. She decides everything. She decided what I'd be called. ...But not this. You're right. Not this.
approve ratatoille +2: You told me my grandmother doesn't get to decide
-> close_end

~ close_end
interject name:ratatoille: Tomorrow I'll do the crust my way. I think I know which way is mine now.
-> END

~ talk_devoted
if name:ratatoille and approval.ratatoille >= devoted and level >= 8
-> devoted
endif
-> END

~ devoted
Narrator: Ratatoille has been unusually quiet for an hour, which means he's planning something. Eventually he presents you, very formally, with a page torn out of his spellbook.
interject name:ratatoille: A recipe. My best one. My grandmother's, actually, with improvements. Many improvements. She'd be furious. It's the bread.
interject name:ratatoille: I've never given anyone a recipe. In my family you inherit them; you don't hand them out. I'm handing it out. To you. Because if anything happens up at that castle, somebody should still be able to make it.
* Nothing's going to happen. -> devoted_nothing
* We'll make it together, after. -> devoted_after

~ devoted_nothing
interject name:ratatoille: Technically, something always happens. But I appreciate the optimism. It's very undercooked. I like it anyway.
approve ratatoille +3: You promised nothing's going to happen to me
-> devoted_end

~ devoted_after
interject name:ratatoille: After. Yes. In a proper kitchen, with a proper oven, and you'll all do it wrong and I'll fix it. That's a deal.
approve ratatoille +3: You promised we'd make the bread together, after
-> devoted_end

~ devoted_end
inspire name:ratatoille: gave away his family's bread
-> END
